{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Phase 1 (Understand) — Root Cause Analysis (rebar-debug)\n\n**Confirmed root cause (mechanism).** The MCP container is deployed by the blue-green\n`docker run` in `mcp_run_new` (`infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh`), which passes BOTH:\n\n- `--env-file \"$COMPOSE_DIR/.env\"` — and `fetch-secrets.sh` writes\n  `REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY=<compose-dir>/rebar-bot-signing-key` (the review-bot HOST key\n  path) into that `.env` (`infra/scripts/fetch-secrets.sh:271`); and\n- `-e REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY=/run/secrets/opcert-ed25519-key`\n  (`infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh:513`).\n\nUnlike `docker compose` — where a service's `environment:` block MERGES OVER `env_file:`,\nyielding a single value — a `docker run` APPENDS both `--env-file` entries and `-e` entries to\nthe container's `Config.Env`. So `REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY` is written TWICE with different\nvalues; the process sees docker's last-wins resolution (the op-cert key), which is correct but\nunasserted. This matches the live inspection recorded in the report exactly (first value =\n`/opt/rebar/infra/compose/rebar-bot-signing-key`, effective = `/run/secrets/opcert-ed25519-key`).\n\n**Why the `.env` value is the dead/wrong duplicate.** The two on-box services need DIFFERENT\nkeys — the review-bot binds `/run/secrets/rebar-bot-signing-key`, the MCP server binds\n`/run/secrets/opcert-ed25519-key` — so a single shared `.env` value cannot own both. Both\ncompose services already declare their own value in their `environment:` block\n(`docker-compose.yml:143` review-bot, `:434` mcp), which overrides `env_file`, so the `.env`\nentry is vestigial: it is overridden in every compose path and is a losing duplicate in the\n`docker run` path. It is the review-bot's HOST path, which does not even exist inside the MCP\ncontainer.\n\n**Defect legitimacy: `defect`** (latent config defect). Cited authority: the ticket ACs + the\ndesign invariant that a signing-key selector must have exactly one owner; the compose merge\nalready realizes per-service single-ownership, and the `docker run` path deviates.\n\n**The fix does NOT change which key signs.** The `-e` op-cert value wins today (verified live)\nand remains the single definition after removing the `.env` duplicate — effective value stays\n`/run/secrets/opcert-ed25519-key`. This is a dead-override removal, not an identity change.\n\n**Caller/scope sweep.** The only consumers of the compose `.env`'s `REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY`\nare the two compose services (both override it) and `mcp_run_new` (also sets it via `-e`). No\nhost-side script sources `.env` for signing. The CI workflows materialize their own key into\n`GITHUB_ENV` independently. Removing the `.env` entry leaves the review-bot unaffected (it keeps\nits `environment:` value + `./rebar-bot-signing-key` bind-mount).\n\n**Defect origin (`caused_by`).** Commit `2a0a4b19f2ab683befae8676e6475bf1b2f43cfc`\n(\"infra: add mcp blue-green autodeploy target\", ticket **6964-40bb-46c9-48a7**) introduced the\n`-e REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY=...` into `mcp_run_new` alongside `--env-file .env` — the change\nthat created the second, colliding definition. The earlier `.env` export (commit `2bbc3ae`,\n2026-07-13, review-bot signing key) was correct-at-the-time single-owner config; the collision\nonly exists because the blue-green `docker run` reproduced the compose env via `-e` without\naccounting for `--env-file`'s non-merging behavior. Close class: `plan_defect`.\n\n**Planned fix (single owning layer = per-service explicit env):**\n1. Remove the `REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY=${signing_key_path}` line (and refresh its stale\n   comment) from `fetch-secrets.sh`'s `.env` heredoc, so `.env` no longer injects a conflicting\n   value into the MCP container. Keep materializing the `rebar-bot-signing-key` file (still\n   bind-mounted + set by the review-bot `environment:`).\n2. Add a regression check (AC #4): render the composed MCP container env (env-file keys ∪ `-e`\n   flags) and assert `REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY` is defined EXACTLY ONCE, with an anti-vacuity\n   anchor (a known-present var proven first) + a mutation-check.\n"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788064826611765448,"uuid":"06053d47-f8cc-4a11-99fc-6737336f1f15"}